# Drive the base to a named location (the skill-level navigate seam, D30/D36).
#
# This is the *semantic* contract: the brain names a location it already knows
# from the world model, never a raw pose or a velocity. The bridge resolves the
# name against the world store, drives Nav2 there, and reports whether the base
# arrived -- so the skill API's `navigate_to(location)` stays exactly the same
# while the classical/real track actually moves (R1).
string location
---
# success=true means the base reached the requested location and the world's
# start_location was updated to match; error is empty.
# success=false means the base did NOT reach the location (unknown name, no
# Nav2 stack, a failed/aborted navigation, ...): error says which.
bool success
string error
---
# No feedback: a semantic location goal has no intermediate progress the brain
# consumes (the bridge owns Nav2's own feedback). Kept deliberately empty so
# the seam exposes nothing but the location and the outcome.
